keating-alias.patch -- the GCC change of 2000-06-23 (Geoffrey Keating), ChangeLog:
    * alias.c (fixed_scalar_and_varying_struct_p): Don't examine struct vs. scalar-ness when
    -fno-strict-aliasing.
It went into GCC 3.0, not into the 2.95 branch.  SN's GPL source of v1.79 still applies the rule; the `path`
library of the game was built with SN BUILD v1.83 (GameCube DWARF), and this is the one code-generation change
that separates v1.83 from the compilers we have.  scripts/replica_v183.py writes the same change into copies of
the official binaries (the function returns NULL at once: with -fno-strict-aliasing, the only setting this
project uses, that is what the change amounts to).  Measured: v1.79 + this patch gives the same assembly as
that three-byte replica on the 27 units of `path` and `rcmp`.

--- a/gcc/alias.c	2026-09-30 19:40:34.733561869 +0200
+++ b/gcc/alias.c	2026-09-30 19:40:34.790339296 +0200
@@ -1215,6 +1215,11 @@
   rtx mem1_addr = XEXP (mem1, 0);
   rtx mem2_addr = XEXP (mem2, 0);
   
+  /* GCC 2000-06-23 (Geoffrey Keating): Don't examine struct vs. scalar-ness when
+     -fno-strict-aliasing.  */
+  if (! flag_strict_aliasing)
+    return NULL_RTX;
+
   if (MEM_SCALAR_P (mem1) && MEM_IN_STRUCT_P (mem2) 
       && !varies_p (mem1_addr) && varies_p (mem2_addr))
